{
  "db_name": "PostgreSQL",
  "query": "-- The unexpired route of the caller's Task of one server on one profile, by the\n-- identifier the server issued. A server issues each Task identifier once, so a second\n-- row means the identifier is ambiguous.\nSELECT\n    r.id,\n    r.tenant AS \"tenant: TenantId\",\n    r.owner AS \"owner: PrincipalId\",\n    r.work_context AS \"work_context: WorkContextId\",\n    r.profile,\n    r.server,\n    r.deployment,\n    r.composition,\n    r.source_task_id,\n    r.authority_digest,\n    p.principal_key AS owner_key,\n    r.owner_kind AS \"owner_kind: PrincipalKind\",\n    r.owner_issuer,\n    r.owner_subject,\n    r.invocation_mode,\n    r.initiator,\n    r.delegation_id,\n    r.data_labels,\n    r.expires_at\nFROM hub.task_route AS r\nJOIN identity.principal AS p ON p.id = r.owner AND p.tenant = r.tenant\nWHERE r.server = $1 AND r.source_task_id = $2 AND r.owner = $3 AND r.profile = $4 AND r.tenant = $5\n    AND r.expires_at > $6\nLIMIT 2\n",
